PROBLEM DEFINITION
We now deﬁne the problem considered in this paper for-
mally. The input to our problem is a set of n d-dimensional
points over positive reals, denoted by D. This set corre-
sponds to the database of ntuples over dattributes. Ad-
ditionally, an integer kwhich speciﬁes the output size is
given. The goal is to ﬁnd a set of tuples, denoted by S,
of size at most kthat minimizes the maximum regret ratio .
Informally, Scorresponds to the set of representative tuples
that will be displayed to the users and the maximum regret
ratio measures how bad the users could feel if they have
to choose from these ktuples instead of the entire database.
We now deﬁne this important concept formally before giving
the precise problem statement.
3.1 Maximum regret ratio
In order to deﬁne this notion, we need to develop the
notions of utility function ,gain, regret, and regret ratio as
follows. (Throughout, we use the car database in Figure 1
as an example.) First, users’ happiness is measured by un-
known utility functions.
